title: Economic Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: economic_policy_timer += 12; month_actions += 1; nationalize_budget = 4; nationalize_budget -= 1 if works_councils >= 2; nationalize_budget -= 1 if works_councils >= 3; nationalize_budget -= 1 if socializations + nationalization_progress >= 2; wtb_budget = 4; wtb_budget -= 1 if works_councils >= 2 or socializations >= 1 or pro_labor >= 2 or debt_brake_reformed
view-if: spd_in_government = 1 and (economic_minister_party == "SPD" or finance_minister_party == "SPD") and economic_policy_timer <= 0 and economic_plan > 0
card-image: img/portraits/SchmidtRobert.jpg

= Economic Policy

The party has adopted an economic plan. Now we have to put it into practice.

- @wtb_2
- @wtb_2_deficit
- @wtb_continuation
- @implement_wtb_no_deficit
- @implement_wtb_deficit
- @nationalize_1
- @nationalize_2
- @moderate_plan
- @moderate_plan_limited_budget
- @root: Do not carry out the economic plan.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

####################### the Zukunftsprogramm (public investment)

@wtb_2
title: Continue the Zukunftsprogramm.
subtitle: -3 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Unemployment is low enough that the programme is no longer needed.
view-if: investment_implemented > 2 and budget >= 3
choose-if: unemployment_rate > 6
on-arrival: works_program += 1; budget -= 3; workers_spd += 5*(1-dissent); unemployment_rate -= 0.7 if unemployment_rate > 6; unemployed_spd += 5*(1-dissent); workers_linke -= 2; workers_afd -= 2; investment_implemented += 1; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; inflation += 0.4; economic_growth += 0.5; economic_growth -= 0.2 if economic_growth > 3

[? if works_program == 4 : The second phase of the Zukunftsprogramm begins. ?][? if works_program > 4 : The Zukunftsprogramm continues. ?] After rail and schools, the money now goes into the industries of the future: battery plants, heat pumps and hydrogen.

@wtb_2_deficit
title: Continue the Zukunftsprogramm.
subtitle: -3 budget. We will run a deficit.
unavailable-subtitle: Unemployment is low enough that we should not borrow for this.
view-if: investment_implemented > 2 and budget < 3 and budget >= -3
choose-if: unemployment_rate > 7
on-arrival: works_program += 1; budget -= 3; workers_spd += 4*(1-dissent); unemployment_rate -= 0.7 if unemployment_rate > 6; unemployed_spd += 4*(1-dissent); workers_linke -= 1; workers_afd -= 1; coalition_dissent += 1; capital_strike_progress += 1; investment_implemented += 1; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; inflation += 0.6; economic_growth += 0.5; economic_growth -= 0.2 if economic_growth > 3

We keep the Zukunftsprogramm going on borrowed money. After rail and schools, the money now goes into the industries of the future.

@wtb_continuation
title: Take stock of the results, and carry on.
view-if: investment_implemented >= 1 and investment_implemented <= 2
on-arrival: budget += 1 if works_program <= 2; unemployment_rate -= 0.8 if unemployment_rate > 5; unemployment_rate -= 0.4 if works_program <= 2 and unemployment_rate > 8; workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 6*(1-dissent); workers_linke -= 2; workers_afd -= 3; works_program += 1; cdu_relation += 3; fdp_relation += 2; coalition_dissent -= 1 if coalition_dissent >= 1; investment_implemented += 1; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if capital_strike_progress >= 3; inflation += 0.3; inflation += 0.2 if unemployment_rate < 5; economic_growth += 0.4; economic_growth -= 0.2 if economic_growth > 3

Construction sites are busy, fewer people claim benefits and tax revenue is up, which pays back part of the cost. We put most of it back into the programme.

The economy is doing better at last. Even some in the Union admit that the money is well spent.

@implement_wtb_no_deficit
title: Launch the Zukunftsprogramm.
subtitle: -[+ wtb_budget +] budget. [? if wtb_budget == 3 : Our earlier reforms have lowered the cost. ?]
unavailable-subtitle: Unemployment is low enough that the programme is no longer needed.
view-if: budget >= wtb_budget and investment_implemented == 0 and investment_adopted == 1
choose-if: unemployment_rate > 6
on-arrival: budget -= wtb_budget; works_program += 1; unemployment_rate -= 1; workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 6*(1-dissent); investment_implemented += 1; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; inflation += 0.4; economic_growth += 0.8; trust_in_democracy += 3*(1-dissent);
achievement: wirtschaftspolitik

The Zukunftsprogramm begins. Money flows into rail lines, power grids, school buildings and social housing across the country.

@implement_wtb_deficit
title: Launch the Zukunftsprogramm.
subtitle: -[+ wtb_budget +] budget. We will run a deficit. [? if wtb_budget == 3 : Our earlier reforms have lowered the cost. ?]
unavailable-subtitle: Unemployment is low enough that the programme is no longer needed.
view-if: budget < wtb_budget and investment_implemented == 0 and investment_adopted == 1
choose-if: unemployment_rate > 6
on-arrival: coalition_dissent += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if fdp_in_government; works_program += 1; budget -= wtb_budget; unemployment_rate -= 1; workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 6*(1-dissent); capital_strike_progress += 1; investment_implemented += 1; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; inflation += 0.6; economic_growth += 0.8; trust_in_democracy += 3*(1-dissent);
achievement: wirtschaftspolitik

We borrow to pay for it. [? if fdp_in_government or cdu_in_government : Our partners are horrified, but the programme goes ahead. ?] Money flows into rail lines, power grids, school buildings and social housing across the country.

####################### the left plan (public ownership)

@nationalize_1
title: Begin the transformation of industry.
subtitle: -[+ nationalize_budget +] budget. [? if works_councils >= 3 : Strong works councils have lowered the cost. ?] [? if socializations >= 2: Our earlier public ownership has lowered the cost. ?]
view-if: nationalization_adopted == 1 and nationalization_progress == 0
go-to: nationalize_deficit if budget < nationalize_budget; nationalize_no_deficit if budget >= nationalize_budget

@nationalize_no_deficit
on-arrival: nationalization_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 2; unemployment_rate -= 0.8 if unemployment_rate >= 5; unemployment_rate -= 0.3 if works_councils >= 3; budget -= nationalize_budget; works_program += 1; workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 4*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1; fdp_relation -= 4; left_dissent -= 5; new_middle_spd -= 2; old_middle_spd -= 3; economy_goal_completed += 1; inflation += 0.4; economic_growth += 0.5 if economic_growth < 3;
achievement: wirtschaftspolitik

[? if nationalization_progress == 1 : A new federal transformation fund takes stakes in steelworks and car suppliers that were about to close[? if works_councils >= 1: , and runs them with their works councils ?]. The plants keep running while they switch to green steel and new products. ?]

[? if nationalization_progress == 1 : The left of the party says that this must only be the beginning. ?]

[? if nationalization_progress > 1 : The fund takes stakes in more companies. A significant part of German industry is now in public hands. ?]

@nationalize_deficit

We do not have the money to buy into the plants. Some want us to borrow for it. Others want us to use Article 15 of the Basic Law, which allows the socialisation of land and the means of production with compensation below market value. Either would be a sharp break with our past.

- @nationalize_deficit_1
- @nationalize_without_compensation
- @empower_workers
- @return: No, we should not do this.

@nationalize_deficit_1
title: Borrow to pay for the transformation fund.
choose-if: left_strength > reformist_strength + center_strength or fahimi_advisor == 1
subtitle: [? if fahimi_advisor: Yasmin Fahimi can win the party over to borrowing for this. ?]
unavailable-subtitle: [? if left_strength <= reformist_strength + center_strength: The party does not yet support borrowing for this. ?] [? if not fahimi_advisor : Perhaps an economic advisor could help win the party over? ?]
on-arrival: nationalization_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 3; unemployment_rate -= 0.7 if unemployment_rate >= 5; unemployment_rate -= 0.3 if works_councils >= 3; budget -= nationalize_budget; works_program += 1; workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 4*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 2; fdp_relation -= 6; cdu_relation -= 4; new_middle_spd -= 3; old_middle_spd -= 3; economy_goal_completed += 1; inflation += 0.6; economic_growth += 0.6 if economic_growth < 3;
achievement: wirtschaftspolitik

We borrow to fill the transformation fund. [? if nationalization_progress == 1 : It takes stakes in steelworks and car suppliers that were about to close[? if works_councils >= 1: , and runs them with their works councils ?]. ?][? if nationalization_progress > 1 : The fund takes stakes in more companies. A significant part of German industry is now in public hands. ?]

@nationalize_without_compensation
title: Use Article 15 of the Basic Law.
subtitle: Socialise the plants with compensation far below market value. This is sure to end up before the Constitutional Court.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if left_strength <= reformist_strength + center_strength: Most of the party does not support this. ?] [? if judicial_reform < 2 : Without legal groundwork, the courts would stop this. ?]
choose-if: left_strength > reformist_strength + center_strength and judicial_reform >= 2
on-arrival: nationalization_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 7; firewall_erosion += 3; unemployment_rate -= 0.6 if unemployment_rate >= 5; unemployment_rate -= 0.3 if works_councils >= 3 and unemployment_rate >= 3; works_program += 1; workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 5*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 2; fdp_relation -= 10; cdu_relation -= 8; greens_relation -= 5; left_strength += 15; reformist_dissent += 10; left_dissent -= 10; new_middle_spd -= 5; old_middle_spd -= 8; economy_goal_completed += 1; linke_relation += 5*(1-dissent); inflation += 0.8; economic_growth += 0.3 if economic_growth < 3;
achievement: wirtschaftspolitik

For the first time, a federal government uses Article 15. The owners call it expropriation, and the Union and the FDP file a complaint in Karlsruhe. But the plants keep running, and their workers keep their jobs.

@empower_workers
title: Hand closing plants to their workers.
subtitle: Give the workforce of any plant that is to be closed the right to take it over as a cooperative, with state guarantees.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if left_strength <= reformist_strength : Most of the party does not support this. ?] [? if judicial_reform < 2 : Without legal groundwork, the courts would stop this. ?] [? if works_councils < 1 : We need stronger works councils first. ?]
choose-if: left_strength > reformist_strength and judicial_reform >= 2 and works_councils >= 1
on-arrival: nationalization_progress += 1; capital_strike_progress += 6; firewall_erosion += 4; unemployment_rate -= 0.7 if unemployment_rate >= 5; unemployment_rate -= 0.3 if works_councils >= 3 and unemployment_rate > 4; works_program += 1; workers_spd += 8*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 6*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 2; fdp_relation -= 10; cdu_relation -= 8; greens_relation -= 5; workers_afd -= 4*(1-dissent); unemployed_afd -= 4*(1-dissent); left_strength += 15; reformist_dissent += 10; left_dissent -= 10; new_middle_spd -= 5; old_middle_spd -= 10; factory_takeovers += 1; economy_goal_completed += 1; linke_relation += 5*(1-dissent); inflation += 0.6; economic_growth += 0.3 if economic_growth < 3;
achievement: wirtschaftspolitik

Workers at closing plants can now take them over, backed by state loans. The business associations call it the end of the social market economy, and the AfD calls it theft. But in the industrial towns of the Ruhr and Saxony, some of its own voters cheer.

@nationalize_2
title: Continue the transformation of industry.
subtitle: -[+ nationalize_budget +] budget. [? if works_councils >= 3 : Strong works councils have lowered the cost. ?] [? if socializations + nationalization_progress >= 2: Our earlier public ownership has lowered the cost. ?]
view-if: nationalization_adopted == 1 and nationalization_progress >= 1
go-to: nationalize_deficit if budget < nationalize_budget; nationalize_no_deficit if budget >= nationalize_budget

####################### the Seeheimer plan (targeted jobs)

@moderate_plan
title: Carry out the targeted jobs plan.
subtitle: -2 budget.
unavailable-subtitle: -2 budget. [? if budget < 2 : We do not have the money. ?] [? if unemployment_rate < 6 : Unemployment is low enough that this is not needed. ?]
view-if: moderate_plan_adopted == 1
choose-if: budget >= 2 and unemployment_rate >= 6
on-arrival: budget -= 2; works_program += 1; unemployment_rate -= 0.7 if unemployment_rate >= 6; inflation += 0.3; workers_spd += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent); rural_spd += 2*(1-dissent); moderate_plan_progress += 1; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; inflation += 0.2 if unemployment_rate < 6; economic_growth += 0.5; trust_in_democracy += 3*(1-dissent);
achievement: wirtschaftspolitik

[? if moderate_plan_progress == 1 : Short-time work is extended, companies that invest get a tax credit, and the hardest-hit regions get money for job programmes. ?][? if moderate_plan_progress > 1 : We extend the targeted jobs plan for another year. ?]

[? if unemployment_rate >= 7 : The Union and the business associations support it as the least bad option. ?][? if unemployment_rate < 7 : Unemployment is already falling, and the plan seems to make little difference. ?]

@moderate_plan_limited_budget
title: Carry out part of the targeted jobs plan, at a lower cost.
subtitle: -1 budget.
unavailable-subtitle: -1 budget. [? if budget < 1 : We do not have the money. ?] [? if unemployment_rate < 6 : Unemployment is low enough that this is not needed. ?]
view-if: moderate_plan_adopted == 1
choose-if: budget >= 1 and unemployment_rate >= 6
on-arrival: budget -= 1; works_program += 1; unemployment_rate -= 0.4 if unemployment_rate >= 6; inflation += 0.2; workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 2*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 1*(1-dissent); rural_spd += 1*(1-dissent); moderate_plan_progress += 1; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; inflation += 0.1 if unemployment_rate < 6; economic_growth += 0.2; trust_in_democracy += 2*(1-dissent);
achievement: wirtschaftspolitik

[? if moderate_plan_progress == 1 : Short-time work is extended and the hardest-hit regions get money for job programmes. ?][? if moderate_plan_progress > 1 : We extend part of the targeted jobs plan for another year. ?]
